    "id": "train-3718",
    "question": "Tom opens an amusement park.  It cost $100,000 to open initially.  It also cost 1% of that to run per day.  He sells 150  tickets a day for $10 each.  How long will it take to make back his money?",
    "gold": "200",
    "answer": "It cost 100,000*.01=$<<100000*.01=1000>>1,000 a day to keep the place open\nHe makes 150*10=$<<150*10=1500>>1500 a day from the park\nSo he makes a profit of 1500-1000=$<<1500-1000=500>>500 a day\nSo it takes 100000/500=<<100000/500=200>>200 days to make back his money\n#### 200"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how long it will take Tom to make back his initial investment of $100,000, we need to calculate his daily profit and then determine how many days it will take to cover the initial investment.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the daily cost to run the amusement park. The initial cost to open the park is $100,000, and it costs 1% of that to run per day. Therefore, the daily running cost is:\n\\[\n0.01 \\times 100,000 = 1,000\n\\]\nSo, the daily cost to run the park is $1,000.\n\nNext, let's calculate the daily revenue from ticket sales. Tom sells 150 tickets a day at $10 each. Therefore, the daily revenue is:\n\\[\n150 \\times 10 = 1,500\n\\]\nSo, the daily revenue is $1,500.\n\nNow, we can calculate the daily profit by subtracting the daily running cost from the daily revenue:\n\\[\n1,500 - 1,000 = 500\n\\]\nSo, the daily profit is $500.\n\nTo find out how many days it will take to make back the initial investment of $100,000, we divide the initial investment by the daily profit:\n\\[\n\\frac{100,000}{500} = 200\n\\]\nSo, it will take 200 days to make back the initial investment.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{200}\n\\]",
